        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8049d64f-aef0-5952-a95a-ec7ebb6c7c13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Republican Party, GOP\n- Laws: Kansas–Nebraska Act, Missouri Compromise\n- People: Stephen A. Douglas, Franklin Pierce\n- Places: Kansas, Nebraska\n- Events: Bleeding Kansas, Pottawatomie massacre\n- Concepts: popular sovereignty\n\nFacts:\n- The Republican Party, also called the GOP for \"Grand Old Party,\" is one of the world's oldest extant political parties.\n- The Republican Party emerged in 1854 to combat the Kansas–Nebraska Act.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act dissolved the terms of the Missouri Compromise and allowed slave or free status in the territories to be decided by popular sovereignty.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act created the territories of Kansas and Nebraska.\n- Democratic Senator Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois and President Franklin Pierce drafted the Kansas–Nebraska Act.\n- Bleeding Kansas was largely brought about by the Missouri Compromise and the Kansas–Nebraska Act.",
